WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:06.440
Hi, welcome back to the Lam Rim (LAM RIM).

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:12.940
Today, we're going to do an episode called 
"Fine Points of my Paradise."

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:24.620
It means you know how to arrange your future paradise quite consciously, carefully, and successfully.

00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:31.100
We're going to start. He's still talking 
about the advantages of vows.

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:38.300
I remember many years ago 
I wanted to become a vegetarian

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:46.220
but I was living in a small Mongolian monastery and there were ten or fifteen 80-year old monks.

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:55.160
They all ate meat and I was the cook, so 
I had to cook and I had to make meat for them.

00:00:55.880 --> 00:01:02.440
I decided I didn't want to eat meat 
but I didn't know how to get out of it.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:08.660
One day I said I had a really bad stomach ache 
and I had to go to doctor. 

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:16.040
Everybody liked this doctor because he charged the monks five dollars--in America!

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:24.180
He was this old, old country doctor. 
Anyway, I drove there in the car and I sat in the car, and I never went into his office.

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:29.720
I waited for about forty-five minutes 
and then I drove back to the monastery.

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:33.680
And I told all the monks--they said, "Are you okay?"

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:40.100
I said, "Yeah, but the doctor said 
I have to give up meat. I can't eat meat anymore."

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:42.840
And they said, "But can you cook it?" 
And I said, "Yeah, yeah, I can cook it.

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:46.560
If you need me to cook it I'll cook it, 
but I can't eat it anymore."

00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:52.880
And they said, "Well, okay," and then I started eating frozen macaroni for the rest of my life.

00:01:53.260 --> 00:01:59.940
But there was a Mongolian geshe, 
a very, very high geshe who was blind.

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:06.000
I was living in the next room and he called me in.

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:11.400
He was very old and blind--high, high geshe.

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:17.080
And he said, "You know giving up meat,
that's a good thing. That's a very good thing."

00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:20.960
"But," he said, "taking a vow would be better."

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:27.820
We arranged a little ceremony. 
I took a little vow from him not to eat meat

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:31.700
and it was something very beautiful.

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:36.060
So that's a little bit about what we're going to talk about--the power of a vow

00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:41.580
and the difference between making a vow to do something and just deciding to do something. 

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:43.160
So here it says..

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:45.320
we're going to go to the text.

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:50.500
so tar gyi dompa ni khen lob gendun dang chepa le khe langpa yinpe
(SO THAR GYI SDOM PA NI MKHAN SLOB DGE 'DUN DANG BCAS PA LAS KHAS BLANGS PA YIN PAS)

00:02:51.000 --> 00:03:01.180
When you take these Pratimoksha (pratimokṣa) vows, 
either lifetime laymen's vows, 
or even just keeping your ten good deeds,

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:10.240
or if you want to go deeper, you can be a novice monk or nun, or an intermediate nun, or a full monk or nun.

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:15.920
And it says here when you take those Vinaya vows,

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:19.740
you take them from khen lob gendun
(MKHAN SLOB DGE 'DUN).

00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:24.580
khen (MKHAN) means Khenpo (MKHAN PO),
which nowadays means "abbott."

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:31.660
But in the ancient Vinaya texts, as those of you who are following the Mixed Nuts classes know...

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:37.580
and by the way, you're always welcome to come to the Mixed Nuts classes. You should find out about them.

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:41.200
They are extraordinary translation classes. 
I think the best in the world.

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:46.840
All the great classics. All the different categories of the great classics at the same time.

00:03:47.180 --> 00:03:52.960
So Khenpo there means the person who 
grants you your vows, your Vinaya vows.

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:57.260
lob (SLOB) means the different lobpuns (SLOB DPON) 
or acharyas (ācārya),

00:03:57.920 --> 00:04:03.100
which means the assistants 
to the person who gives you your Vinaya vows.

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:07.940
If you're becoming a monk or a nun, 
there's the vow giver 

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:16.040
and then there are several main guys who help with the ordination, and they're called  lobpun.

00:04:16.420 --> 00:04:21.620
And then gendun (DGE 'DUN) means you have to have enough monks there to make a new monk

00:04:22.020 --> 00:04:26.960
and there are certain requirements about a quorum, 
or how many monks should be there.

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:29.124
dang chepa le ke langpa
(DANG BCAS PA LAS KHAS BLANGS PA)

00:04:29.124 --> 00:04:39.160
So when you take these Vinaya vows, you have taken them from these--I don't know--five, six people at least. Sometimes many more.

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:44.220
dey lab ja dang galway dik tung shakpay tse
(DE'I BSLAB BYA DANG 'GAL BA'I 
SDIG LTUNG BSHAGS PA'I TSE')

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:50.400
And then when you break 
those commitments you made--

00:04:50.600 --> 00:05:01.420
and those could be breaking commitments that you made, sort of general commitments like "I think I won't like to eat meat,"

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:07.240
or tungwa (LTUNG BA)
which means more formal commitments that you took.

00:05:07.660 --> 00:05:10.460
But if you break them, 
shakpay tse-ang (BSHAGS PA'I TSE'ANG),

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:14.160
when you clean yourself,

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:20.680
shakpa (BSHAGS PA) means when you open your heart and you tell someone else about the mistake you made,

00:05:20.680 --> 00:05:24.320
which is a very important element 
of cleaning a karmic seed.

00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:31.740
When you break it, 
when you open your heart and admit what you did--

00:05:32.180 --> 00:05:33.360
shakpay tse-ang--

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:35.840
gendun gyi dun du shak gu,
(DGE 'DUN GYI MDUN DU BSHAGS DGOS)

00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:44.560
you should try to do it in the presence of some of the people that you took the vows from.

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:47.840
And that's why living in a monastery is so powerful.

00:05:47.840 --> 00:05:53.500
Because when you get there 
you take certain vows from certain people

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:58.000
and then you're living around those 
people for the rest of your life.

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:00.580
Oftentimes those people are with you 
for the rest of your life.

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:09.000
And so they are always available
for you to go into their room and say, "Look, 
I made a mistake today. I broke my vows."

00:06:09.380 --> 00:06:14.960
And I apologize to the person who gave me those vows. So that's very powerful.

00:06:15.160 --> 00:06:17.820
gu kyi, rang chik pur shakpe
(DGOS KYI, RANG GCIG PUR BSHAGS PAS)

00:06:18.380 --> 00:06:24.940
Is it an option to just sit in your room 
and sort of make a little confession?

00:06:25.540 --> 00:06:30.920
"I broke my vow today. I did this mistake.

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:33.880
I broke this vow and I'm very sorry

00:06:33.880 --> 00:06:37.000
and I'll try to control myself in the future."

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:41.840
The text here, Pabongka Rinpoche says, 
"Is that enough?"

00:06:42.060 --> 00:06:46.840
He says, "Well, it depends on what you did."

00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:55.920
Meaning if you just broke some general rule of morality, then maybe that's okay

00:06:56.320 --> 00:07:01.220
to just sit in your room and make a sincere confession.

00:07:01.960 --> 00:07:03.660
Out loud helps.

00:07:03.920 --> 00:07:07.760
Promise not to do it again. 
Do your four powers.

00:07:08.320 --> 00:07:12.800
You will be able to clean that negative seed.

00:07:13.100 --> 00:07:14.380
But. He says kyang (KYANG),

00:07:14.380 --> 00:07:17.120
tungwa dak mi tubpe
(LTUNG BA 'DAG MI THUB PAS)

00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:25.440
If you took a specific vow from another person,
and I think implied here is that they are still available,

00:07:25.680 --> 00:07:29.720
then you should go to them 
and you should tell them, "I broke my vow."

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:32.080
Otherwise, you won't be able to clean it completely.

00:07:32.260 --> 00:07:35.160
Okay, so that's a pretty strong statement.

00:07:36.040 --> 00:07:45.120
When you break a vow that you took from somebody then really you should go to that person and explain to them what you broke. 

00:07:45.120 --> 00:07:53.340
Or a similar person. 
A similar person of seniority or integrity. 
You go and confess it to them.

00:07:53.540 --> 00:07:58.820
And he says that that is the only way 
you will be able to clean that seed completely.

00:07:59.360 --> 00:08:05.280
Now there is a tradition, 
like for example in your bodhisattva vows,

00:08:05.980 --> 00:08:12.200
to confess to a Buddha statue on your altar 
or something like that.

00:08:12.280 --> 00:08:17.280
And that's okay. If you don't have any choice. 
Like if you're in a three-year retreat or something,

00:08:17.800 --> 00:08:22.520
and you're not seeing anybody, 
then obviously that would be appropriate.

00:08:22.840 --> 00:08:29.060
And if you can't get to somebody else 
to confess that would be appropriate.

00:08:29.060 --> 00:08:35.620
But we have this very powerful desire inside of us.

00:08:36.340 --> 00:08:42.300
I think I have it very strong. 
I want other people to like me.

00:08:42.300 --> 00:08:44.480
I want other people to think I'm a good person.

00:08:45.180 --> 00:08:49.720
It pains me if someone sees me 
doing something wrong.

00:08:50.200 --> 00:08:54.740
And so, I think like many of us, I try to hide it. It's called chabpa ('CHAB PA).

00:08:54.740 --> 00:08:59.880
I try to hide my mistakes. 
And there's a joke...

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:09.140
There's a joke that we often spend more effort to hide the things we did wrong

00:09:09.380 --> 00:09:13.600
than we do to fix it. 
Or not to do it. Or just stop doing it.

00:09:13.910 --> 00:09:17.800
We spend much more effort 
trying to hide the things we do.

00:09:17.800 --> 00:09:22.600
So I just wanted to say here,
I think it's a good place to add that

00:09:22.600 --> 00:09:30.020
if you can, then tell somebody else. 
Anybody else, okay?

00:09:30.100 --> 00:09:32.100
Tell someone else.

00:09:32.640 --> 00:09:39.760
You know, there's a requirement: they have to be a human being, they have to have ears, they have to understand your language, obviously.

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:47.100
Tell somebody and then the bad seed
is much, much less. 

00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:53.800
We have a picture here.  
I found this picture of a lady who went to the store.

00:09:53.800 --> 00:09:58.420
She's buying something special at the store.

00:09:58.620 --> 00:10:07.360
This is a kind of a weird box. 
I don't know why she's buying it, but she likes it.

00:10:08.440 --> 00:10:13.800
Certain items in an American store...
let's say it's a chain store,

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:16.800
there may be thirty stores,

00:10:16.800 --> 00:10:18.980
if it's a strange item like this box,

00:10:19.140 --> 00:10:23.460
you have to take it back to the store 
where you bought it. 

00:10:23.740 --> 00:10:26.800
If you don't like it, you can't take it to a branch store.

00:10:27.160 --> 00:10:32.800
You have to take it back to the store where you bought it, and that reminds me of this idea.

00:10:33.320 --> 00:10:39.660
If it's possible then go back to the person 
that you took the vows from.

00:10:40.420 --> 00:10:44.880
If you break them, go back to them 
and tell them when you break them.

00:10:44.880 --> 00:10:49.380
And that says something about how you take vows. 

00:10:49.380 --> 00:10:57.700
You can take vows--bodhisattva vows, tantric vows--you can take them from a famous lama

00:10:58.100 --> 00:11:04.660
or from some famous teacher who comes 
and is teaching a hundred people or a thousand people or ten thousand people.

00:11:05.000 --> 00:11:10.900
They're offering vows.
You can take vows from them and it feels like an honor.

00:11:11.200 --> 00:11:18.760
But there's a tradition that it's good to take your vows from someone who lives near you,

00:11:19.160 --> 00:11:22.140
if you can, from someone in the same community.

00:11:22.880 --> 00:11:28.040
Then when you break them you can go back 
to the store where you bought the vows

00:11:28.180 --> 00:11:32.520
and you can clean them more effectively because they're going to watch you in the future.

00:11:32.800 --> 00:11:37.840
You know, my lama, 
I lived with him for almost thirty years,

00:11:38.840 --> 00:11:43.380
I really did try to go to him and confess.
I would knock on his door.

00:11:43.880 --> 00:11:47.200
The first few times he listened to me very carefully.

00:11:47.500 --> 00:11:50.160
And he said, "Okay, don't do that again."

00:11:50.920 --> 00:11:58.440
Later, it got to be so common for him that 
I would open the door and say that I have to talk to you and he would say, "I know, I know.

00:11:59.120 --> 00:12:07.060
It's clear, you know. 
I even know which one you broke, I can tell!"

00:12:07.660 --> 00:12:14.440
I'd say, "I'm sorry" and I always felt much better.

00:12:14.900 --> 00:12:22.540
I think in the end it worked for me that 
I got rid of my bad habits by being open with him. 

00:12:23.020 --> 00:12:26.880
So I really encourage you to do it.

00:12:30.440 --> 00:12:37.160
Now Pabongka Rinpoche starts talking 
about the small things.

00:12:38.160 --> 00:12:42.180
There's this expression in American English,
"It's all in the details."

00:12:43.060 --> 00:12:46.520
It's all in the small things, you know, and it says here

00:12:46.520 --> 00:12:54.660
dey nang ne kyang (DE'I NANG NAS KYANG)--
If you consider all the different Vinaya vows or commitments that you can take,

00:12:54.660 --> 00:12:57.140
there are some tiny, tiny...

00:12:57.760 --> 00:13:05.720
they almost don't even count as vows; they're just kind of strong suggestions at the end of the smallest vows.

00:13:06.220 --> 00:13:16.760
chab len (CHAB LEN) means, 
try to rinse your mouth after you take your meals 
so you don't get bad breath and hurt people.

00:13:17.160 --> 00:13:24.380
And hlam phu (LHAM PHUD)... 
hlam (LHAM) means "shoes," 
so take your shoes off when it is appropriate,

00:13:24.380 --> 00:13:30.980
like when you enter a temple, 
or when you're going to sit down on a meditation mat, especially somebody else's meditation mat.

00:13:32.200 --> 00:13:39.860
tsun ni chepa (TSUN MI BYED PA)--
Suppose you didn't do that,
you broke those tiny suggestions.

00:13:39.860 --> 00:13:48.700
gu phu dung chen gyon gu jung (GOS PHU DUNG CAN GYON DGOS BYUNG)--
or some small thing where you had to 
kind of fudge your Vinaya vows.

00:13:49.060 --> 00:13:59.420
So a monk is not supposed to wear clothes with sleeves on them. We're supposed to always wear sleeveless tops,

00:13:59.740 --> 00:14:04.160
called a tungak (STOD 'GAG)
We're supposed to always wear those.

00:14:04.160 --> 00:14:10.700
Now every monk I know, if it's cold, 
if you're in Mongolia and it's snowing,

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:15.220
they will put on a jacket.

00:14:15.520 --> 00:14:19.440
Technically a jacket is not allowed in the Vinaya.

00:14:19.440 --> 00:14:23.560
But the Vinaya was written for central India 
where it never snows.

00:14:23.680 --> 00:14:34.340
So these small things, small suggestions that we are supposed to keep if we want to be really careful.

00:14:35.260 --> 00:14:39.500
So Rinpoche wants to talk about those and he says,

00:14:39.560 --> 00:14:43.800
de le hlakpa rung mi nupa per je ne
(DE LAS LHAG PA BSRUNG MI NUS PA 
DPER BYAS NAS)

00:14:44.000 --> 00:14:47.420
Or it could be something else similar to that.

00:14:48.100 --> 00:14:51.780
But if you find that you can't keep those things--nang chung mi ja (MNANGS CHUNG MI BYA)

00:14:52.600 --> 00:15:02.420
Don't take it lightly. Don't blow it off. 
Okay, maybe you have to put a jacket on 
if you are a monk in Mongolia.

00:15:02.660 --> 00:15:07.620
Maybe you have to. But don't blow it off. 
Don't think it's not important.

00:15:07.800 --> 00:15:15.440
Don't think you shouldn't follow that rule where you can and still keep yourself healthy, okay?

00:15:16.240 --> 00:15:20.600
So don't blow off even these tiny suggestions.

00:15:20.780 --> 00:15:25.520
nang chung mi ja...
phem hlak sok le (PHAM LHAG SOGS LAS)--

00:15:25.520 --> 00:15:29.700
You can take pampa shi (PHAM PA BZHI)
hlak ma bcu gsum (LHAG MA BCU GSUM)... 

00:15:29.700 --> 00:15:32.360
these are different levels of vows.

00:15:32.800 --> 00:15:34.860
phampa (PHAM PA) is the first level of vows.

00:15:35.100 --> 00:15:37.640
hlak ma (LHAG MA) is the second level of vows.

00:15:38.020 --> 00:15:45.700
phampa means, literally, "destroyed." 
Your vow is destroyed if you commit it, 
like killing a human being.

00:15:45.940 --> 00:15:52.880
And then hlakma means you don't lose all your vows, but you lose a lot.
You still have a little bit left.

00:15:53.280 --> 00:15:55.280
le (LAS)--
so these are the very serious monk's vows.

00:15:56.260 --> 00:16:00.100
tramo gong mu de dak tenpay mik tu la nu tsab chewa yin
(PHRA MO GONG SMOS DE DAG BSTAN PA'I MIG LTOS LA GNOD TSABS CHE BA YIN)

00:16:00.800 --> 00:16:05.020
This is an interesting concept.

00:16:08.120 --> 00:16:10.120
One point of view, one...

00:16:10.360 --> 00:16:17.020
one state of mind that a monk or nun especially, or someone who took bodhisattva vows,

00:16:17.560 --> 00:16:22.140
one thing we have to keep in mind is 
"how do we look to other people?"

00:16:22.140 --> 00:16:25.200
Not in an egotistical way.

00:16:25.600 --> 00:16:30.560
But we have to think, if you're a spiritual person,

00:16:31.040 --> 00:16:39.380
then it is important, and it is useful to think how do you appear to other people.

00:16:39.380 --> 00:16:42.820
I live in America. 
Buddhists are very uncommon.

00:16:42.820 --> 00:16:44.320
We are not common.

00:16:44.329 --> 00:16:49.238
Some of my neighbors found out I'm a Buddhist, 
so now they are watching me.

00:16:49.459 --> 00:16:56.858
They are very traditional Christians and they are watching me because for them I am Buddhism.

00:16:57.200 --> 00:17:00.860
See what I mean? 
For my neighbours, I am Buddhism.

00:17:00.860 --> 00:17:08.640
So if I act in a nice way they will have respect for Buddha and that would be a good seed for them.

00:17:08.960 --> 00:17:14.240
And if I make small mistakes, 
you see because small mistakes are... 

00:17:14.280 --> 00:17:24.580
what Pabongka Rinpoche is saying here, 
small mistakes give people impressions 
almost easier than big mistakes.

00:17:24.800 --> 00:17:33.420
In my neighborhood, I think if they found out I had stolen things from the store as a kid,

00:17:33.700 --> 00:17:37.340
and I had a police record, 
I think they wouldn't mind so much.

00:17:37.800 --> 00:17:41.840
Because many people in my community 
have these kind of small police records.

00:17:42.460 --> 00:17:49.060
But if I leave my garbage can 
out on the street for an extra day,

00:17:49.060 --> 00:17:54.300
they'll say, "Buddhists are bad people, 
Buddhists are not good people.

00:17:54.300 --> 00:17:58.220
They leave their garbage can out too long."

00:17:58.700 --> 00:18:03.480
I think what Pabongka Rinpoche 
is saying here is very interesting.

00:18:03.480 --> 00:18:12.540
That it's the small things that give other people impressions of you and of the path you are practicing.

00:18:12.560 --> 00:18:21.560
If you say, "I'm a lam rim practitioner, 
I'm following the lam rim, 
I'm going to all the online lam rim events,

00:18:21.560 --> 00:18:25.260
I'm becoming a lam rim master," which you can online.

00:18:25.260 --> 00:18:28.580
I guess, cool, because you get to see it 
over and over if you want to. 

00:18:28.580 --> 00:18:35.000
Then you have to kind of watch 
how you behave with the small things.

00:18:35.060 --> 00:18:37.920
Okay? With the small things.

00:18:38.700 --> 00:18:45.289
And then Pabongka Rinpoche takes this discussion 
in a very interesting direction.

00:18:45.660 --> 00:18:50.700
It's kind of like DCI. Like a good DCI teaching.

00:18:51.260 --> 00:18:55.900
He takes this discussion in an interesting direction.

00:18:56.180 --> 00:18:59.160
He says, "Okay, let's suppose you don't...

00:18:59.480 --> 00:19:04.018
you're a monk and you don't rinse your mouth 
out after you take your meal."

00:19:04.020 --> 00:19:10.760
You you can see the picture here 
of this businessman who didn't brush his teeth, 

00:19:11.180 --> 00:19:17.780
and then he came to the office 
and he is reading this thing out loud 

00:19:18.860 --> 00:19:24.160
and he smells really bad, 
his breath smells really bad to the assistant.

00:19:24.220 --> 00:19:28.820
He's not even aware of it. 
He's not thinking about it. It's a small thing.

00:19:29.100 --> 00:19:34.020
It's not a big thing. 
But Pabongka Rinpoche says, 

00:19:34.720 --> 00:19:38.440
pang tung jinlab sok kyang chi nu kyi che
(SPANG LTUNG BYIN RLABS SOGS 
KYANG CI NUS KYIS BYED)

00:19:39.040 --> 00:19:43.560
But you should go through--

00:19:43.840 --> 00:19:51.000
there are steps for a monk to clean away 
even small bad seeds.

00:19:51.000 --> 00:19:59.060
pang tun (SPANG LTUNG) means these are not very serious vows, these are not heavy vows.

00:19:59.080 --> 00:20:01.800
They are serious, but they are not heavy.

00:20:02.020 --> 00:20:07.420
There are ways to remove the bad seed which is 
jinlab (BYIN RLABS), which is a blessing.

00:20:07.440 --> 00:20:15.280
These are ways to reduce the bad seeds 
from breaking smaller vows.

00:20:16.160 --> 00:20:18.540
chi nu kyi che (CI NUS KYIS BYED)--

00:20:18.940 --> 00:20:25.580
You should try really hard to purify even those small seeds when you make a mistake.

00:20:26.780 --> 00:20:35.340
If you go to work without brushing your teeth and you are killing your assistant with your bad breath 

00:20:35.340 --> 00:20:40.480
and you realize it, then you should do something to remove that tiny bad seed.

00:20:40.520 --> 00:20:41.740
Why?

00:20:41.740 --> 00:20:46.140
jikten di na gung tsik dang ja sok sopa la-ang
('JIG RTEN 'DI NA GUNG TSIGS DANG 
JA SOGS BZO PA LA'ANG)

00:20:46.960 --> 00:20:54.420
Even in the normal world--
and that's a common scriptural sentence opener.

00:20:54.760 --> 00:21:00.620
Even in the normal world. 
Forget Buddhist monastery. Forget Lam Rim retreat.

00:21:00.620 --> 00:21:03.600
Even in the normal world--jikten di na ('JIG RTEN 'DI NA)--
in this world.

00:21:03.960 --> 00:21:10.620
gung tsik (GUNG TSIGS) means fixing something for "lunch," cooking something for lunch.

00:21:11.380 --> 00:21:17.780
And ja (JA) means making yourself a coffee. 
But it's "tea," which is Tibetan coffee.

00:21:18.120 --> 00:21:21.860
Which makes me thirsty.

00:21:21.860 --> 00:21:27.060
sopa la-ang (BZO PA LA'ANG)
You want to make a good tea?
And by the way tea is the...

00:21:28.060 --> 00:21:31.080
like coffee is the foundation of American culture,

00:21:32.360 --> 00:21:36.420
salt tea is the foundation of Tibetan culture.

00:21:36.420 --> 00:21:44.520
And the first thing that happened to me 
when I got to the monastery was,  
well first of all, the new guys have to be the cooks.

00:21:44.520 --> 00:21:49.180
So I was assigned to be a cook the first day. 
I was the cook for eight years.

00:21:49.580 --> 00:21:52.820
It was good for me. Good for my pride.

00:21:53.500 --> 00:21:57.800
So they're going to teach me 
how to make a nice Tibetan tea.

00:21:58.180 --> 00:22:03.600
To make a Tibetan tea, it's a hard thing to do, 
it's not an easy thing to do.

00:22:04.020 --> 00:22:05.660
It's got to have salt,

00:22:05.660 --> 00:22:06.690
butter,

00:22:06.690 --> 00:22:07.810
soda,

00:22:07.810 --> 00:22:09.010
nutmeg,

00:22:09.010 --> 00:22:10.180
milk,

00:22:10.180 --> 00:22:12.180
cream,

00:22:12.660 --> 00:22:13.880
Chinese black tea,

00:22:14.400 --> 00:22:16.660
and then you have to use a ja dong (JA DONG).

00:22:16.660 --> 00:22:21.460
You have to use a... what do you call those things?  Butter... churn! You have to use a churn.

00:22:22.000 --> 00:22:24.929
It takes a long time and it's a hard thing to do.

00:22:24.929 --> 00:22:31.140
It's a hard thing to do right, a good Tibetan tea. 
And my lama drank about twenty-five cups a day.

00:22:31.720 --> 00:22:33.440
So I was in the kitchen a lot.

00:22:33.440 --> 00:22:39.380
But when you make that tea, 
you've got to have all the ingredients.

00:22:39.380 --> 00:22:44.340
And again, the taste of a good Tibetan tea 
is in the details.

00:22:44.760 --> 00:22:48.960
The taste of a good tea is in the details.

00:22:49.340 --> 00:22:56.120
Did you crush the salt carefully? 
Himalaya rock salt. Did you crush it carefully?

00:22:56.120 --> 00:23:01.000
Did you get the best kind of spices that you could?

00:23:01.380 --> 00:23:07.060
Did you use a very good block of black tea?

00:23:07.380 --> 00:23:12.920
Did you not overcook it? 
But did you let it steep long enough?

00:23:13.680 --> 00:23:19.560
Even when you're cooking a lunch or you are making a tea for your teacher, for example,

00:23:20.100 --> 00:23:29.260
the difference between a normal cup of tea and an extraordinary cup of tea is in the small details.

00:23:29.260 --> 00:23:31.560
It's not some big grand thing.

00:23:31.980 --> 00:23:34.560
Why is Pabongka Rinpoche talking about that?

00:23:35.420 --> 00:23:41.280
What he's saying is what makes the difference between a normal spiritual person

00:23:41.940 --> 00:23:47.860
and a really special spiritual person is the small things, it's the small details.

00:23:47.940 --> 00:23:51.520
So he says don't blow off these little vows.

00:23:52.600 --> 00:23:59.560
If you've made a commitment to open doors for people, then for the rest of your life open doors for people.

00:23:59.560 --> 00:24:05.680
If you made a commitment to serve a beverage 
to someone in the room first,

00:24:06.000 --> 00:24:11.520
then you're going to do it for the rest of your life, 
and don't blow off these small commitments.

00:24:11.520 --> 00:24:17.420
What we see here is a Christmas tree decoration.

00:24:18.240 --> 00:24:24.360
I like to call it 
"finishing touches on a perfect world."

00:24:24.700 --> 00:24:28.780
So don't forget, what we're doing--

00:24:29.200 --> 00:24:33.340
especially after you learn the pen and 
after you learn the four steps--

00:24:33.340 --> 00:24:37.400
what a lam rim person is trying to do.

00:24:37.800 --> 00:24:42.120
We're trying to design our future Buddha paradise.

00:24:42.600 --> 00:24:47.640
It's not like an expensive penthouse 
in Manhattan or Paris.

00:24:48.480 --> 00:24:52.260
It's not like that. Don't think of it like that.

00:24:52.720 --> 00:24:57.180
It's a perfect world. 
It's the mandala (maṇḍala) that you offer before class.

00:24:58.020 --> 00:25:05.020
You are trying to build, piece by piece, a perfect world.

00:25:05.400 --> 00:25:13.060
That's what the steps on the path is all about. 
Each step is another seed to plant a perfect world,

00:25:13.740 --> 00:25:19.420
perfect galaxy, a perfect universe. 

00:25:19.420 --> 00:25:23.200
That's what we're doing 
and that comes from the small things.

00:25:23.420 --> 00:25:27.420
That comes from taking care 
about what kind of salt you buy,

00:25:27.640 --> 00:25:30.700
making sure the butter is fresh for the butter tea.

00:25:30.880 --> 00:25:37.920
Making sure you really work hard to find the best water for the tea, which is very, very important.

00:25:37.920 --> 00:25:43.100
Making sure the presentation of the tea is very elegant.

00:25:43.740 --> 00:25:48.580
It's in the small things that you build a Buddha paradise.

00:25:48.760 --> 00:25:52.199
That's why I was showing a Christmas tree.

00:25:52.840 --> 00:26:03.620
In my family when I was growing up, it was a big thing. We would get a license from the government to go out in the forest and cut a Christmas tree.

00:26:03.720 --> 00:26:09.400
We would carry it home, it was a lot of work, 
and then we would set it up.

00:26:10.179 --> 00:26:13.889
All the kids would put the decorations on the tree.

00:26:14.470 --> 00:26:18.797
I still do it. Veronica loves these Christmas trees.

00:26:18.800 --> 00:26:24.200
And then there's the last bulb you put on the tree. 

00:26:24.200 --> 00:26:29.420
Somehow you look at the tree. 
You've been working on it for two, three hours.

00:26:29.640 --> 00:26:34.040
And then you say it needs one more bulb 
and you put the last bulb on the tree.

00:26:34.440 --> 00:26:37.480
Then it's like, 
"Wow! Now it's perfect!"

00:26:37.860 --> 00:26:49.920
So don't forget that brushing your teeth may be the final bulb on the Christmas tree of your Buddha paradise.

00:26:49.940 --> 00:26:53.040
Don't blow off even small, small things.

00:26:53.040 --> 00:27:01.640
If something will bring comfort or happiness 
to another living being, then do it.

00:27:02.280 --> 00:27:08.000
Because your Buddha paradise 
is made from the small touches.

00:27:08.280 --> 00:27:11.380
Pabongka Rinpoche is saying

00:27:11.700 --> 00:27:15.800
don't blow off these little vows, 
don't blow off these little commitments.

00:27:16.000 --> 00:27:22.049
Don't blow off the littlest commitments you take 
with your bodhisattva vows or your tantric vows.

00:27:22.660 --> 00:27:27.800
Never blow them off because those are the finishing touches on your Buddha paradise. 

00:27:27.800 --> 00:27:34.220
You won't have a complete Buddha paradise 
unless you really watch the small things.

00:27:34.720 --> 00:27:40.160
And the small things are what other people remember, not the big things.

00:27:40.680 --> 00:27:44.160
So if your goal is to make other people happy,

00:27:44.460 --> 00:27:50.000
really, most often, it's the small things 
that make people happy, 
not the grand gestures.

00:27:50.640 --> 00:27:53.360
It's the small things that make people happy.

00:27:53.980 --> 00:27:58.080
rang re chi mar dun du nyer ja'i ten drubpa la-ang
(RANG RES PHYI MAR DON DU 
GNYER BYA'I RTEN SGRUB PA LA'ANG)

00:27:58.720 --> 00:28:02.440
Now, he doesn't get into Buddha paradises,

00:28:02.860 --> 00:28:08.300
He says, "You also need the small touches 
to get a human body next time."

00:28:09.160 --> 00:28:17.040
I've got this image of Pabangka Rinpoche saying, 
"Look, watch out for the small things.

00:28:17.040 --> 00:28:22.400
You don't brush your teeth one day 
and maybe you don't have an ear in your next life."

00:28:22.400 --> 00:28:29.440
Maybe you get a body without an ear or maybe your nose is going to be twisted like a U or something.

00:28:29.440 --> 00:28:37.240
You've got to be careful because it's the little things that you do now that create every detail of your future body. 

00:28:37.240 --> 00:28:44.700
I think the human body has about thirty-thousand working parts. 
I believe it's about thirty-thousand working parts.

00:28:44.700 --> 00:28:54.600
And it's a miracle that those parts are working together, like a fine Swiss watch like my friend makes.

00:28:58.120 --> 00:29:00.120
He's Mr. Hess... Walter.

00:29:02.700 --> 00:29:06.900
It's the small things that make it work,

00:29:07.180 --> 00:29:14.780
and each one of those thirty-thousand pieces in the human body that you have was created by many small karmas.

00:29:15.860 --> 00:29:22.640
So if you're thinking about continuing this spiritual journey, which is always a multi-life task--

00:29:22.640 --> 00:29:30.520
if you're in the Lam Rim course now and if you think ten years is a lot that we've been studying lam rim, 

00:29:30.520 --> 00:29:33.800
 
this is at least a five-hundred year project.

00:29:34.620 --> 00:29:37.940
I'm impressed by the government of China.

00:29:38.040 --> 00:29:41.180
They always have a five-year plan. 
They always have a ten-year plan.

00:29:42.639 --> 00:29:48.239
My government, to be honest, we don't even have 
a five-day plan or a ten-day plan.

00:29:49.360 --> 00:29:53.759
But if you're a lam rim citizen,

00:29:55.020 --> 00:29:59.580
you have at least a five-hundred year plan, 
maybe a thousand-year plan.

00:30:00.040 --> 00:30:09.360
Which means you're going to have to have 
at least seven to ten bodies.

00:30:09.880 --> 00:30:14.480
So we have to be careful to design our body.

00:30:14.480 --> 00:30:16.580
So he's not talking Buddha paradise right now.

00:30:16.580 --> 00:30:23.940
He says you have to watch the small things because they're going to help you come back in a body

00:30:24.500 --> 00:30:28.520
which has ears and a nose, 
where there's Dharma and things like that.

00:30:29.280 --> 00:30:31.860
ten druppa la-ang tsultrim sungwa dang
(RTEN SGRUB PA LA'ANG TSUL KHRIMS 
BSRUNG BA DANG)

00:30:32.160 --> 00:30:34.220
jinpa tangwa sok na re michokpe
(SBYIN PA BTANG BA SOGS SNA RES MI CHOG PAS)

00:30:35.140 --> 00:30:43.800
To get that perfect body, you're going to have to have morality, but you're also going to have to do the bodhisattva perfections.

00:30:43.800 --> 00:30:45.040
What are they?

00:30:45.100 --> 00:30:47.100
Giving.

00:30:48.060 --> 00:30:51.740
Morality. Being a good person. 
Being nice to other people.

00:30:52.240 --> 00:30:54.520
Not getting angry.

00:30:54.760 --> 00:30:58.120
Having fun when you film Lam Rim.

00:30:58.580 --> 00:31:01.040
Meditation, and wisdom.

00:31:01.580 --> 00:31:08.020
He says, "Look, you guys have your sights 
on those high bodhisattva things,

00:31:09.340 --> 00:31:13.180
but the foundation is always being nice to other people."

00:31:13.180 --> 00:31:15.260
You can be very generous,

00:31:15.540 --> 00:31:18.780
you can be practicing the six perfections,

00:31:18.780 --> 00:31:25.980
you can have this bodhisattva intention, you can be practicing with emptiness understanding,

00:31:26.260 --> 00:31:31.860
but if you don't have morality, that's empty. 
It's all empty. It's all fake.

00:31:31.860 --> 00:31:34.900
It doesn't have a strong foundation to it.

00:31:34.900 --> 00:31:44.460
If you're not being nice to other people, it doesn't matter how great a scholar you are, or a meditator, 
it doesn't matter. It's hollow.

00:31:44.460 --> 00:31:49.800
tsultim tsanway ngu ne, jin tong sok kyang gang drub che gu
(TSUL KHRIMS GTZANG BA'I NGOS NAS, SBYIN GTONG SOGS KYANG GANG 'GRUB BYED DGOS)

00:31:49.880 --> 00:31:54.240
So do your high bodhisattva works, 
do your high tantric things,

00:31:54.540 --> 00:31:59.860
but make sure the foundation is being nice to other people in the grocery store.

00:32:00.500 --> 00:32:12.760
ga shik gi, so tar gyi dulway chupa ni, wangpo menpa nam kyi chu yul yin gyi,
wang nun yang rab nam kyi, dendray gu dok che migupar
('GA' ZHIG GIS, SO THAR GYI 'DUL BA'I SPYOD PA NI, DBANG PO DMAN PA RNAMS KYI SPYOD YUL YIN GYI, DBANG RNON YANG RAB RNAMS KYIS, DE 'DRA'I GU DOG BYED MI DGOS PAR)

00:32:13.020 --> 00:32:16.920
So now he addresses a common misperception.

00:32:17.340 --> 00:32:25.660
And he says, "Look, you see people around who say, 'Oh, those Vinaya vows, all those-- who can count them?

00:32:25.660 --> 00:32:28.520
Monk's vows, nun's vows,

00:32:28.520 --> 00:32:33.280
combined it's over five hundred, six hundred vows. 
It's too much.

00:32:33.520 --> 00:32:45.500
That kind of very practical guidance, like what to eat, what to wear, how to clean your room,

00:32:46.040 --> 00:32:52.420
this is for lower lam rim practitioners.

00:32:52.640 --> 00:32:58.120
That's really for lower people. 
That's for people who are kind of clueless.

00:32:58.160 --> 00:33:07.280
This heavy Vinaya stuff, that's really made for people who are not very sophisticated.

00:33:07.640 --> 00:33:13.380
This is probably made for yak herders 
or cow herders in India.

00:33:13.480 --> 00:33:19.620
Clean your room and put your water bowls
and all this kind of stuff.'"

00:33:20.240 --> 00:33:23.320
He says: wang nun yang rab nam kyi
(DBANG RNON YANG RAB RNAMS KYIS)

00:33:24.000 --> 00:33:36.720
"'Us higher practitioners, 
us more sophisticated practitioners 
who have a higher normal IQ and a higher spiritual IQ,'"

00:33:36.720 --> 00:33:38.720
gu dok che
(GU DOG BYED)

00:33:38.760 --> 00:33:41.980
"'This is just a hassle. An unnecessary hassle.

00:33:42.240 --> 00:33:48.180
The Vinaya was created for simple people 
and I'm not a simple person.

00:33:48.450 --> 00:33:51.074
I'm a sophisticated modern person.

00:33:51.080 --> 00:33:56.800
I understand the Vinaya was useful 
for village people in India.

00:33:56.800 --> 00:34:04.780
But look, I'm living in Manhattan and we are sophisticated.'" Paris. Beijing. Shenzhen.

00:34:05.120 --> 00:34:06.240
"'We are sophisticated.'"

00:34:06.420 --> 00:34:07.320
Guadalajara.

00:34:07.580 --> 00:34:11.800
"'We don't need this. We need higher stuff.

00:34:12.440 --> 00:34:14.260
We need the higher stuff.'"

00:34:14.300 --> 00:34:17.340
gu dok che-- 
"'that's just a pain in the butt, that stuff.'"

00:34:17.520 --> 00:34:20.100
migupar sang ngak kyi nyur lam
(MI DGOS PAR GSANG SNGAGS KYI MYUR LAM)

00:34:20.100 --> 00:34:25.380
"'Ah, now tantra, the way of the secret word,

00:34:25.880 --> 00:34:29.771
this is the real fast track. I'm a fast track person.'"

00:34:29.771 --> 00:34:31.900
duk sum lam khyer
(DUG GSUM LAM 'KHYER)

00:34:31.900 --> 00:34:38.340
"'In fact, as I understand it...'" by the way this is a wrong view. 
I'm just repeating a wrong view.

00:34:38.760 --> 00:34:42.740
"'As I understand it,'" 
duk sum lam khyer

00:34:43.320 --> 00:34:52.020
"'you can use the three poisons of the mind in tantra 
as a rocket ship to higher goals. 

00:34:52.440 --> 00:34:54.140
You can use anger.

00:34:54.380 --> 00:34:56.380
You can use sex.

00:34:56.380 --> 00:35:04.040
You can even use your misunderstandings 
as a rocketship. That's the special quality of tantra.'"

00:35:04.260 --> 00:35:11.340
Don't take this statement out of context from the video. I'm just translating.

00:35:11.960 --> 00:35:15.900
He says you meet this 
che-pe chok che
(BYED PAS CHOG CES)

00:35:15.900 --> 00:35:24.060
You see people saying, "That's enough. I'm this elegant... I'm this sophisticated diamond way practitioner.

00:35:24.060 --> 00:35:31.340
I'm not like those village people who need to be told how 
to clean their room and how to put out their water bowls and stuff like that.

00:35:31.460 --> 00:35:34.900
I'm on a fast-track."
labpa la chir yang mi tsiway
(BSLAB PA LA CIR YANG MI BRTZI BA'I)

00:35:35.520 --> 00:35:37.520
Then you see them,

00:35:38.520 --> 00:35:40.520
and they get worse and worse.

00:35:40.520 --> 00:35:44.600
They say, "Oh, alcohol is a path in the diamond way.

00:35:45.100 --> 00:35:47.100
I will take a drop."

00:35:47.100 --> 00:35:49.100
Then the next day, "I will take a sip."

00:35:49.299 --> 00:35:53.489
Then the next week they need a bottle, 
and I've seen people like this.

00:35:53.489 --> 00:35:57.700
I've really seen people like this 
and they have ruined their life

00:35:58.120 --> 00:36:04.300
by misusing diamond way ideas, 
misusing diamond way substances.

00:36:04.300 --> 00:36:06.280
I have seen it.

00:36:06.540 --> 00:36:10.260
And they just ruined their life. 
Okay, they just ruined their life.

00:36:10.600 --> 00:36:14.740
chupar che mu
(SPYOD PAR BYED MOD)
He says you see people like that. 
There are people like that.

00:36:15.480 --> 00:36:18.140
But sang ngakpa yin yang (GSANG SNGAGS PA YIN YANG),

00:36:18.860 --> 00:36:22.480
But I'll tell you something.
You can be a diamond way practitioner,

00:36:23.000 --> 00:36:25.880
so tar gyi dom den yin na
(SO THAR GYI SDOM LDAN YIN NA)

00:36:26.140 --> 00:36:35.620
But you must keep your Vinaya vows. 
You must keep your ten good deeds, 
because that's the engine that drives tantra.

00:36:36.180 --> 00:36:39.420
Well-kept Vinaya vows,

00:36:39.420 --> 00:36:46.800
well-kept bodhisattva vows, are the engine that drives tantra, that drives the diamond way.

00:36:46.820 --> 00:36:48.400
Okay, so don't blow it off.

00:36:48.500 --> 00:36:58.100
Don't say, "I'm a beyond that," and especially don't make the mistake of using substances--alcohol, meat, sex--

00:36:58.360 --> 00:37:02.520
and thinking that this is going to... 
you're so high. 

00:37:02.520 --> 00:37:05.420
You can just do these things. You can use anger.

00:37:05.540 --> 00:37:11.780
I have a picture here of a guy, he's like, "I'm Yamantaka!

00:37:11.780 --> 00:37:19.760
When I'm at work I use my tantric practice. 
I yell at people and I visualize myself as a blue creature

00:37:20.000 --> 00:37:25.820
with twelve arms and I'm yelling at everybody, 
but it's really just a tantric practice.

00:37:25.980 --> 00:37:29.500
I have this high tantric practice going on."

00:37:29.860 --> 00:37:35.320
And he says, "Forget that!"
Pabongka Rinpoche says, "Forget that!"

00:37:35.320 --> 00:37:39.020
You see people acting like that and they are deluded.

00:37:40.040 --> 00:37:41.620
Why?

00:37:41.620 --> 00:37:47.520
sang ngakpa yin yang so tar gyi dom den yin na tsul shin sung gu te, pungsang gi gyu le
(GSANG SNGAGS PA YIN YANG SO THAR GYI SDOM LDAN YIN NA TSUL BZHIN BSRUNG DGOS TE, DPUNG BZANG GI RGYUD LAS)

00:37:47.700 --> 00:37:56.520
Then he quotes a famous tantra, which is called pung sang gi shupa shejaway gyu (DPUNG BZANG GIS ZHUS PA ZHES BYA BA'I RGYUD)

00:37:57.200 --> 00:38:06.060
It's a tantra. 
It's a famous tantra called, "The Questions of Subahu." The person's name was Subahu, 
and here's the quotation.

00:38:06.260 --> 00:38:08.260
Who's talking?

00:38:08.320 --> 00:38:13.620
It's a tantra. Who taught it? 
Lord Buddha in his highest form.

00:38:15.280 --> 00:38:18.160
Lord Buddha in this high, high form.

00:38:18.540 --> 00:38:22.240
He says,
gyelwa nge sung so so tarpa yi,
(,RGYAL BA NGAS GSUNGS SO SO THAR PA YI,)

00:38:22.240 --> 00:38:24.740
tsultrim namdak dulwa ma lu le,
(,TSUL KHRIMS RNAM DAG 'DUL BA MA LUS LAS,)

00:38:25.160 --> 00:38:27.900
ngakpa kyimpe tak dang choga pang,
(,SNGAGS PA KHYIM PAS RTAGS DANG CHO GA SPANG,)

00:38:28.200 --> 00:38:30.660
hlakma nam ni nyam su langwa ja
(,LHAG MA RNAMS NI NYAMS SU BLANG BAR BYA,)

00:38:30.660 --> 00:38:38.300
It is a very powerful statement.  
He says, "Look, I am the Buddha."

00:38:38.300 --> 00:38:43.040
So I'm giving you the Buddha's... the straight dope, 
the straight word from the Buddha.

00:38:43.240 --> 00:38:45.000
I'm giving you the straight word from the Buddhas.

00:38:45.000 --> 00:38:46.380
so so tarpa yi
(SO SO THAR PA YI)

00:38:46.620 --> 00:38:53.600
"I taught those Vinaya vows. 
Those basic, basic foundational vows.
I taught them.

00:38:53.960 --> 00:39:01.140
If you happen to be a tantrika, 
you are following the diamond way,

00:39:01.140 --> 00:39:05.920
and you happen to be not a monk or nun,

00:39:05.940 --> 00:39:14.640
the only Vinaya things I allow you not to keep, 
are the robes and the monk's rituals." 
Got it?

00:39:14.660 --> 00:39:27.740
"If you are a layperson and you take tantric vows, the only Vinaya things I allow you not to follow is monk's robes and the monk's special rituals."

00:39:27.760 --> 00:39:30.620
They have different kinds of water pots 
and stuff like that.

00:39:30.800 --> 00:39:38.300
But the rest you have to keep. 
In other words, except for your clothing, "I expect you to be a monk or a nun.

00:39:38.300 --> 00:39:44.960
You want to be a tantrika? 
Then I expect you to be a monk or a nun on the inside.

00:39:44.960 --> 00:39:49.080
On the outside you can still wear a suit and tie.

00:39:49.080 --> 00:39:54.180
But on the inside if you want to practice tantra 
you have to keep this basic vows,

00:39:54.180 --> 00:39:57.300
you have to follow these basic guidelines

00:39:57.380 --> 00:40:00.880
that I have laid out for you in the Vinaya."

00:40:01.710 --> 00:40:04.879
Alright, we ran over a little bit. 
I apologize.

00:40:05.940 --> 00:40:09.140
Sometimes Pabongka Rinpoche 
just has a little bit more to say.

00:40:10.480 --> 00:40:17.180
And I think it's really beautiful this idea 
that if we watch the small things

00:40:17.760 --> 00:40:20.040
that will make other people happy

00:40:20.400 --> 00:40:24.480
we are putting the finishing touches 
on our Buddha paradise.

00:40:24.900 --> 00:40:26.094
Okay, cool.

00:40:26.094 --> 00:40:28.700
See you next time.
Thank

00:40:35.820 --> 00:40:37.820
You.

